From: osy <osy@turing.llc>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 18:40:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-gpu: enable render server for Venus/Neptune on macOS

virtio_gpu_virgl_init() gated VIRGL_RENDERER_RENDER_SERVER behind
#ifndef CONFIG_METAL, so on macOS (CONFIG_METAL defined) the flag was
never set. This virglrenderer build serves Venus/Neptune exclusively
out-of-process via the render-server proxy, so without the flag
proxy_renderer_init() never runs, state.proxy_initialized stays false,
and virgl_renderer_fill_caps(VENUS) leaves the capset zeroed. The guest
Mesa Venus driver then reports "Unsupported wire format version 0" and
vkEnumeratePhysicalDevices fails, leaving llvmpipe as the only device.

Set VIRGL_RENDERER_RENDER_SERVER unconditionally for venus/neptune.
With this, the render servers spawn at init and the guest enumerates the
Venus physical device (Virtio-GPU Venus, DRIVER_ID_MESA_VENUS).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-4-8

(cherry picked from utmapp/qemu commit 268dee8834; ui/console API renamed for 11.1)
---
 hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
index ecc0e7483e0..80998969014 100644
--- a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
+++ b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
@@ -1551,9 +1551,7 @@ static int virtio_gpu_virgl_init(VirtIOGPU *g)
 #if VIRGL_VERSION_MAJOR >= 1
     if (virtio_gpu_venus_enabled(g->parent_obj.conf)) {
         flags |= VIRGL_RENDERER_VENUS;
-#ifndef CONFIG_METAL /* Metal does not support render server */
         flags |= VIRGL_RENDERER_RENDER_SERVER;
-#endif
     }
     if (virtio_gpu_drm_enabled(g->parent_obj.conf)) {
         flags |= VIRGL_RENDERER_DRM;
@@ -1578,9 +1576,7 @@ static int virtio_gpu_virgl_init(VirtIOGPU *g)
 #ifdef VIRGL_RENDERER_NEPTUNE
     if (virtio_gpu_neptune_enabled(g->parent_obj.conf)) {
         flags |= VIRGL_RENDERER_NEPTUNE;
-#ifndef CONFIG_METAL
         flags |= VIRGL_RENDERER_RENDER_SERVER;
-#endif
     }
 #endif
 
